# Allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# Listing things to exclude means naming them, and this file is
# committed. An allowlist keeps the build context to exactly what the
# runtime needs and says nothing about anything else on disk.
#
# node_modules is deliberately absent: the image installs its own with
# `npm install --production`, so the host copy (which carries esbuild
# and the CodeMirror sources) must never be copied over it.

*

!server.js
!lib/
!public/
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# Build inputs stay out; the built bundle lives in public/js/vendor
# and is covered by the rule above.
public/js/vendor/*.map
